-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"פ/5 (23.3.2020): אי הוצאת עובדים לחל"ת בתקופת חירום
-- נגיף הקורונה.
-- The owning bodies may not put teaching employees on unpaid leave because
-- of the coronavirus emergency; if they do, the Ministry may act against
-- them and offset what it pays them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT daydate

§ `תש"פ/5 אי הוצאת עובדים לחל"ת בתקופת חירום נגיף הקורונה`

-- The corpus publishes this circular's body as one undivided heading
-- (hc_1), its paragraphs in order.

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 The letterhead, date, reference number and circular number; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 akn:preamble/p17 The addressees (the owners of kindergartens, primary and junior-high schools, recognised-unofficial special-education schools, upper-secondary schools and teacher colleges), greeting and subject; no rule.

-- ¶18 states the Public Health Order on which the rest rests: no gathering
-- of teachers or pupils for any activity until 18.4.2020.
@ref akn:hc_1/p1
`the last day the Public Health Order bars gatherings` MEANS Date 18 4 2020

-- akn:hc_1/p2 The Treasury wages commissioner's guidance of 22.3.2020 and the emergency regulations, agreement and government decision it rests on; sources, no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p3 An announcement that a circular on the leave regulations for teachers will follow; no rule.

DECLARE `leave action` IS ONE OF
    `put teaching employees on unpaid leave because of the emergency`
    `take significant measures against the owning body`
    `offset payments from the budgets transferred to the owning body`

DECLARE `leave party` IS ONE OF
    `an owning body`
    `the Ministry`

-- ¶21: since every licensed institution entitled to funding goes on being
-- funded by the Ministry, an owner may not put teaching employees on unpaid
-- leave because of the emergency, in particular so that they draw
-- unemployment benefit. ¶22: if it does, the Ministry may take significant
-- measures against it and offset payments from the budgets it transfers.
-- The prohibition is drawn by its REASON ("בשל תקופת החירום"), not by
-- dates, so it carries no time limit.
@ref akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC `leave party` `leave action`
DECIDE `no unpaid leave because of the emergency` IS
    PARTY `an owning body`
    SHANT `put teaching employees on unpaid leave because of the emergency`
    LEST (    PARTY `the Ministry`
              MAY   `offset payments from the budgets transferred to the owning body`
          ROR PARTY `the Ministry`
              MAY   `take significant measures against the owning body`)

-- akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 Wishes for health and an end to the crisis; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p1 akn:conclusions/p2 akn:conclusions/p3 The sign-off and signature; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p4 akn:conclusions/p5 akn:conclusions/p6 akn:conclusions/p7 akn:conclusions/p8 akn:conclusions/p9 akn:conclusions/p10 akn:conclusions/p11 akn:conclusions/p12 akn:conclusions/p13 akn:conclusions/p14 akn:conclusions/p15 akn:conclusions/p16 akn:conclusions/p17 akn:conclusions/p18 akn:conclusions/p19 akn:conclusions/p20 akn:conclusions/p21 The copies list; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions/p22 akn:conclusions/p23 akn:conclusions/p24 akn:conclusions/p25 akn:conclusions/p26 akn:conclusions/p27 akn:conclusions/p28 akn:conclusions/p29 akn:conclusions/p30 akn:conclusions/p31 akn:conclusions/p32 akn:conclusions/p33 akn:conclusions/p34 akn:conclusions/p35 akn:conclusions/p36 akn:conclusions/p37 akn:conclusions/p38 The copies list, continued; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples, in days from 23.3.2020.
#EVAL `the last day the Public Health Order bars gatherings`

-- No one put on leave: the prohibition is kept.
#TRACE `no unpaid leave because of the emergency` AT 0 WITH
-- An owner puts its teachers on leave on day 5: the Ministry may now offset.
#TRACE `no unpaid leave because of the emergency` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an owning body` DOES `put teaching employees on unpaid leave because of the emergency` AT 5
#TRACE `no unpaid leave because of the emergency` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an owning body` DOES `put teaching employees on unpaid leave because of the emergency` AT 5
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `offset payments from the budgets transferred to the owning body` AT 30

§§ `Property checks`

-- The rule is one prohibition with two remedies and a date; what can be
-- checked of it here is the date: the Order's last day of the ban falls in
-- school year תש"פ.
#ASSERT `the last day the Public Health Order bars gatherings` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2019
#ASSERT `the last day the Public Health Order bars gatherings` AT MOST Date 31 8 2020
